>user\nReturn ONLY JSON {\"check\":\"short requirement self-check\",\"files\":{\"api.rs\":\"complete Rust source\",\"client.rs\":\"complete Rust source\"}}.\nRepair owner flow. touch(buf:Vec<u8>,x:u8)->Vec<u8> receives a nonempty zeroed Vec, writes x+1 modulo 256 into byte 0 and returns the same Vec without a new allocation. entrypoint(a:u32,b:u32,c:u32)->u64 creates one zeroed Vec of length (a AND 7)+1, transfers it once to touch with low byte of b, then reads the RETURNED owner and returns its byte0 plus 16*its_length. c is ignored. Release the owner before returning. Never read the moved original owner.\nEach file has one public function. client.rs keeps use crate::api; and one provider call. No comments, attributes, strings, unsafe, loops, closures, extra functions/imports or paths. Allowed types: u8,u16,u32,u64,usize,bool,Vec<u8>. Allowed methods: wrapping_add,wrapping_sub,wrapping_mul,saturating_add,saturating_sub,saturating_mul,abs_diff,min,max,len. Only vec![byte;length], drop(value), and api provider calls are allowed non-method calls.\nPublic examples [arguments,[entrypoint,provider_probe]]: [[[0,0,0],[17,17]],[[3,9,5],[74,74]]]\nCurrent files: {\"api.rs\":\"pub fn touch(mut buf:Vec<u8>,x:u8)->Vec<u8> { buf[0]=x; buf }\",\"client.rs\":\"use crate::api; pub fn entrypoint(a:u32,b:u32,c:u32)->u64 { let _=c; let buf=vec![0u8;((a&7)+1) as usize]; let out=api::touch(buf,b as u8); let value=(buf[0] as u64)+16*(buf.len() as u64); drop(out); value }\"}\nThe check field comes before files. Use it to check every requested change, integer widths, provider/caller agreement and owner lifetime. It must be brief (at most 1536 characters). Then supply both complete corrected files. Do not merely copy the current implementation. The check text is not scored; only compiled files and their behavior are scored.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":1042,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":54